WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.160
This is a synthetic study voice. Choose the file format for the work you need

00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:08.320
to do. Keep an editable master and a checked reading copy.

00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:12.880
A DOCX document lets you revise words, headings and tables. Use it for an

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:17.440
editable notice. Open the saved file and check its contents.

00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:21.473
An XLSX workbook can keep sheets and formulas. Change an input, inspect the

00:00:21.473 --> 00:00:25.505
formula and check that the total recalculates.

00:00:25.505 --> 00:00:29.863
A PDF is a page based reading copy. Check every page for missing rows or cut

00:00:29.863 --> 00:00:34.220
off words. Keep the editable source as well.

00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:38.718
A quantity changes. Which file should you update first: the working workbook

00:00:38.718 --> 00:00:43.215
or its old PDF copy? Pause and explain your choice.

00:00:43.215 --> 00:00:48.565
[Pause to answer]

00:00:48.565 --> 00:00:51.890
Update the working workbook. Check the formulas and total, then create and

00:00:51.890 --> 00:00:55.215
inspect a fresh reading copy. Keep the old version so the change can be

00:00:55.215 --> 00:00:58.540
traced.
